# The name stage's did-you-mean, where a name resolves to nothing: the names
# near it, asked of `resolve/asked.hero`, which answers a question asked
# before as it was (design.md §4.17; defect 386), and each one offered
# remembered, so the unused rule stays quiet about it (§4.4).
#
# Moved out of `resolve/state.hero` on 2026-10-07, when the answers it keeps
# took that file past its decided ceiling: the scope stack and the
# resolver's working state stay there, and this is what the name stage does
# with them for a name nothing answers.

use resolve/state
use resolve/asked

# The candidates for a name that resolved to nothing, remembered so the
# unused sweep can stay quiet about them — keyed by the module that was
# offered the repair, so a did-you-mean in geom.hero cannot exempt a name
# in main.hero (a dropped error, 2026-08-12). The candidates are lists read
# one after another, never joined (defect 385).
function near_names(@r: state.Resolver, name: str, candidates: [[str]]) -> [str]
    near = asked.nearest(@r.asking, name, candidates)

    for candidate in near
        state.keyed_add(@r.suggested, module: r.module, name: candidate)

    return near
